{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["Their kinswomen — their sisters, a plural form. 'Shimon and Levi are brothers' means: Shimon and Levi were brothers in doing evil." "Weapons of violence — Their sisterhood: מכרותיך and מולדתיך are a term for kinsfolk. But מְכֵרוֹתֵיהֶם is a doubled-letter form (mishkal degash), like מסיבותיהם — a term for kinship, except that the resh in place of the chirik turns into a tzeirei — it is a small qamatz, like בֵּרֵךְ instead of בִּרֵךְ, אִבֵּד and שִׁבֵּר. And likewise: חֶרֶף י׳. And שָׁרַת אֶת אֶחָיו — all of them are doubled-letter forms (mishkal degash). מכרותיהם — parenté in the vernacular."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {1 "The lemma 'כלי חמס' appears to have been assigned to this comment by the editor though the comment's content returns to interpreting מכרותיהם from the preceding verse; the final phrase 'לוד פרנטייש' is textually difficult, possibly a garbled form of Old French 'parenté' (kinship)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:40.509667037Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}